// Connections closed for a revoked access before their session.ended reached the transport.
// Backs the "revocations close connections untold" alert: before the hub aborts a deactivated
// user's connections it sends each one session.ended, so the client stops reconnecting and says
// why. Each close is tagged with whether its own send went through, so a told connection on one
// instance never hides an untold one: any untold access-revoked close means the send failed or
// stalled (on Azure SignalR Service, the service refused or could not be reached) and that client
// saw its connection drop without a reason. Any such window is worth a look.
customMetrics
| where name == "tellma.realtime.closes"
| extend reason = tostring(customDimensions["reason"])
| extend told = tostring(customDimensions["told"])
| where reason == "access-revoked" and told == "false"
| summarize untold = sum(valueSum) by cloud_RoleInstance, bin(timestamp, 15m)
| where untold > 0
